
Developer Build Workflow (GitHub/GitLab) – Detailed Class Notes

The image illustrates the Developer Build Process. This process is followed by developers to build, test, and upload code to a Git repository (GitHub or GitLab) before it enters the CI/CD pipeline.

What is a Developer Build?

A Developer Build is the process performed in a developer's local machine (Developer Workspace) where source code is compiled, tested, packaged, and then pushed to a version control system like GitHub or GitLab.

The main objective is to ensure the code is working correctly before it is shared with the team.

