The image appears to show part of a CI/CD (Continuous Integration/Continuous Deployment) pipeline, specifically the build process. Here's what each stage means:

GitLab → Clone
The CI pipeline starts by cloning the latest source code from the GitLab repository.
Nightly Build
An automated build that runs every night (or on a scheduled basis) to verify that the latest code integrates successfully.
Source Code
The project's source files (e.g., Java files).
Compilation
The source code is compiled into object files or Java bytecode (.class files).
This step checks for syntax and compilation errors.
Object Files
The compiled output generated by the compiler.
Packaging
The compiled files and required resources are bundled into deployable artifacts.
Deliverables
The final packaged artifacts, such as:
JAR (Java Archive) – Used for Java libraries or standalone Java applications.
WAR (Web Application Archive) – Used for Java web applications deployed to application servers like Tomcat.
